  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.5251 acc, clearly showing that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted is the strongest architecture pattern. Transformer aggregation (config_013) underperformed and was expensive (12.31 GPU hrs), so the remaining lever for improvement is the image encoder. Question: Does upgrading from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-Large (imagenet_vit_l) improve accuracy while keeping the proven avgpool+weighted fusion? This directly isolates the image-encoder effect on the best-known configuration. Why this experiment: It is the most logical exploitation of the current best result with a single high-impact change. The expected cost is moderate (~6-9 GPU hours, higher than the 4.42 for ResNet50 due to ViT-L's larger parameters, but well below the 12+ GPU hours of transformer aggregation). With 5 experiments remaining, spending one moderate-cost experiment to test whether a stronger image encoder breaks past the 0.525 ceiling is the best risk/reward tradeoff. If it succeeds, subsequent experiments can refine around it; if it fails, we learn the image encoder is not the bottleneck and can pivot to RNA encoder alternatives (e.g., config_020 or config_031) in the remaining budget."
}

